Here's a Rust function that parses a CSV line into fields, handling quoted commas, along with unit tests using the `rstest` and `csv` crates. This implementation supports quoted fields with commas inside them, as per the standard CSV format.

---

### ✅ Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following crates in your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[dependencies]
csv = "1.1.6"
rstest = "0.16.0"
```

---

### 📜 `src/main.rs`

```rust
use csv::ReaderBuilder;
use rstest::rstest;
use std::io::Cursor;

/// Parses a CSV line into fields, handling quoted commas.
pub fn parse_csv_line(line: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut reader = ReaderBuilder::new()
        .has_headers(false)
        .from_reader(Cursor::new(line));
    let mut fields = Vec::new();

    for result in reader.records() {
        if let Ok(record) = result {
            fields.push(record.iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(","));
        }
    }

    fields
}

#[rstest]
#[case::empty_line("")]
